Objective (s): TO REPRESENT THE FLOW OF INFORMATION WITHIN THE HOSPITAL MANAGEMENT SYSTEM USING DATA FLOW DIAGRAMS AT LEVEL 0, LEVEL 1 AND LEVEL 2.
•	INTRODUCTION TO DATA FLOW DIAGRAM :-
A Data Flow Diagram (DFD) is a graphical representation of how data moves through a system. Level 0 presents the complete system as one process and shows interaction with external entities. Level 1 decomposes the system into major processes, while Level 2 further expands one selected process into smaller subprocesses and data flows. The diagrams show external entities, major system processes, data stores, and movement of information between them.
•	COMPONENTS OF DATA FLOW DIAGRAM :-
Component	Description
Process	Transforms input data into output data (rounded rectangle, numbered such as 1.0, 2.0).
Data Flow	An arrow that shows the movement of information between entities, processes and data stores.
Data Store	A place where data is stored (for example D1 Patient Data).
External Entity	A person or system outside HMS that sends data to or receives data from the system.

