2) Receptionist : Exchanges appointment and bill information with HMS (and gives booking details at Level 2).
3) Doctor : Receives patient/appointment information and the appointment schedule.
4) Admin : Receives reports and system information.
5) Staff : Sends requests to the Prescription process (Level 1).
Processes in the diagram :-
1) Level 1: 1.0 Patient, 2.0 Appointment, 3.0 Admission, 4.0 Prescription, 5.0 Billing, 6.0 Reports & AI.
2) Level 2: 2.1 Book Appointment, 2.2 Check Availability, 2.3 Confirm / Update.
Data stores in the diagram :-
1) D1 Patient Data: Stores patient information.
2) D2 Appointment Data: Stores appointment records (read/written by the Appointment processes).
3) D3 Hospital Records: Stores hospital records used by Reports & AI.
•	CONCLUSION: The DFDs clearly represent information movement in the Hospital Management System. Level 0 gives the overall context, Level 1 shows the major functional processes, and Level 2 explains appointment processing in greater detail.
